      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/8d6153e0-4dc4-4ec5-aeaf-0d12e64a467f)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**Functionality**\nThe test aims to verify SRAM MPU protection by attempting to write and read from code RAM. There is a potential logic flaw in `test_run_step1` where the test might not be marked as failed if the expected reboot doesn\u0027t happen but other assertions fail. Additionally, the test expects a reboot on READ, while a WRITE fault is typically expected for memory protection.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency**\nThe code follows the general pattern for EC multi-step tests. There is a minor naming inconsistency between `test_run_step1` and `run_test_step2`.\n\n**Testing**\nThe CL introduces a new test and integrates it into the build system and `run_device_tests.py`, which is excellent.\n\n**Overall Quality**\nThe CL is a valuable addition to ensure memory protection is working as expected. Addressing the logic in the multi-step state machine will make the test more robust against false positives.",
      "revId": "8189659ee91bf7cfe9425b72d5f42fd10f0021c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c58fcf26_26a48282",
        "filename": "test/sram_mpu_protection.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T18:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Is it intended that the READ (second `memcpy`) causes the reboot? Usually, if the SRAM is protected, the WRITE (line 64) should trigger a data access violation fault and reboot the system. If the write succeeds but the read faults, that would imply the region is Write-Only or has very specific MPU settings.",
      "revId": "8189659ee91bf7cfe9425b72d5f42fd10f0021c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6132fbb8_df46aa88",
