      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T18:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `test_reboot_to_next_step` is called in both branches of the `if`. In the `else` case, if the error count is 0, it reboots to `TEST_STATE_STEP_2`. However, at line 91, `test_set_next_step(TEST_STATE_STEP_2)` was already called. `test_reboot_to_next_step` usually performs a reboot. Is a reboot intended here even if the test passed without one?",
      "revId": "8189659ee91bf7cfe9425b72d5f42fd10f0021c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
